# The key of an identity you register in Studio:
#   Registry -> Agents -> Inventory -> Register Identity.   Shown once, on creation.
#
#   REQUIRED  for the two Strands notebooks, which read it from the environment.
#   OPTIONAL  for langgraph_agent_identity.ipynb, which prompts for it with getpass when unset so
#             the key never lands in the notebook's saved output. Set it here to skip the prompt.
#
# The identity's authority ceiling is the credential policy you attach at registration
# (Registry -> Policies -> Create Policy, then pick it in the Register Identity form).
#
# That policy needs the `nhi:manage` scope for the key to register anything at all -- leave it
# out and the key works right up until the first registration, which fails with
# `403 token missing nhi:manage scope`.
#
# The LangGraph notebook uses this identity as the ORCHESTRATOR (sub type `orchestrator`), so
# its policy also needs every scope it will delegate onward: tools:read tools:execute orders:read
# kb:read. A scope missing there is narrowed out of the specialist's credential silently, with no
# error.
HIGHFLAME_API_KEY=

# --- LangGraph notebook: which model to call --------------------------------

# Optional. The chat model the agents call. Defaults to gpt-4o-mini.
# MODEL_ID=gpt-4o-mini

# Required for the LangGraph notebook: the model its agents call.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# This notebook calls the provider directly. To put the model call itself behind Highflame, run
# langgraph_gateway_agent_identity.ipynb, which uses the variables in the next section.

# --- LangGraph gateway notebook: the model call through the AI gateway -------
#
# langgraph_gateway_agent_identity.ipynb routes every model call through the Highflame AI
# gateway, which does the checking; the agent carries no Highflame code.
# Hosted: https://gateway.highflame.ai/llm/v1.   Self-hosted: http://<host>:8090/llm/v1.
# HIGHFLAME_GATEWAY_BASE_URL=https://gateway.highflame.ai/llm/v1

# Required for the gateway notebook. Forwarded upstream as `Authorization: Bearer`; the gateway
# injects no provider key of its own. A model inside your network that takes no key still needs
# a value here -- any non-empty string.
# PROVIDER_API_KEY=

# Optional. provider/model, as the gateway names it. Defaults to openai/gpt-4o-mini. A model
# behind an OpenAI-compatible server is openai/<its name>.
# GATEWAY_MODEL_ID=openai/gpt-4o-mini

# Optional. Where the gateway notebook's telemetry step reads decisions from. Defaults to
# HIGHFLAME_BASE_URL, which is right for the hosted product; a self-hosted Observatory is its
# own endpoint.
# HIGHFLAME_OBSERVATORY_URL=http://localhost:8092

# --- Self-hosted Highflame (optional) --------------------------------------
#
# Set BOTH of these together. Setting only the base URL sends guardrail calls to your
# deployment while the token exchange still goes to the hosted service, and a self-hosted
# key fails there with "401 invalid api key". The token URL is derived from the identity
# URL unless you override it.
#
# HIGHFLAME_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8070
# HIGHFLAME_IDENTITY_URL=http://localhost:8051
# HIGHFLAME_TOKEN_URL=

# --- Strands notebooks: AWS Bedrock ----------------------------------------

# Optional. AWS profile for Bedrock (for example an SSO profile). Unset = default credential chain.
# AWS_PROFILE=my-sso-profile

# Optional. Unset = Strands' default Bedrock model.
# BEDROCK_MODEL_ID=

# Optional. An IAM role each agent assumes for its Bedrock calls, under its own identity name,
# so CloudTrail attributes model calls to the same agent Highflame does.
# AGENT_ROLE_ARN=arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/highflame-demo-agent

# Optional. S3 bucket where Strands persists the multi-agent conversation.
# SESSION_BUCKET=my-agent-sessions

# Optional. Local port for the A2A server in the swarm notebook.
# A2A_PORT=9910

# Optional. Add AWS region.
# AWS_REGION=
